From: op15-bringup
Subject: [PATCH] BaseMode: stamp IS_OPLUS_PACKAGE for the system camera too

The OnePlus provider (libextensionlayer ExtensionPluginBase::InitPackageName,
read at configure) only grants the Oplus SAT-Fusion config when the client is
first-party Oplus: it sets gate *(plugin+0x36F0) = (com.oplus.packageName in
oplus-list) OR (com.oplus.is.sdk.camera.package tag set). CustomPipelineSelect
then picks OplusSATFusionOfflineReprocess (gate=1) vs the bare
OplusSATOfflineReprocess (gate=0 -> configureStreams INTERNAL_ERROR / -38).

OCS BaseMode only stamps IS_OPLUS_PACKAGE for NON-system-camera (3rd-party) apps
(`if (!Util.isSystemCamera() && useOplusCameraCase()) set(IS_OPLUS_PACKAGE,{1})`),
because stock relies on the OnePlus framework/cameraserver to first-party-tag the
system camera. AOSP (LineageOS) cameraserver does not do that tagging, so the
system camera (com.oplus.camera) is treated as non-Oplus and the SAT session
fails to configure (-38). Make the system camera self-identify.

smali (com/oplus/ocs/camera/producer/mode/BaseMode.smali, "configure" case):
nop the `!Util.isSystemCamera()` guard so the system camera also stamps the tag
(gated only by useOplusCameraCase(), true for rear_sat). Keeps isSystemCamera()
== true elsewhere (so the CaptureResult metadata-pin path is unaffected).

--- a/smali/com/oplus/ocs/camera/producer/mode/BaseMode.smali
+++ b/smali/com/oplus/ocs/camera/producer/mode/BaseMode.smali
@@ (configure case, :pswitch_399)
     invoke-static {}, Lcom/oplus/ocs/camera/common/util/Util;->isSystemCamera()Z
     move-result p2
-    if-nez p2, :cond_3ae
+    nop
     invoke-virtual {p0, p3}, Lcom/oplus/ocs/camera/producer/mode/BaseMode;->useOplusCameraCase(Ljava/lang/String;)Z
     move-result p2
     if-eqz p2, :cond_3ae
     sget-object p2, Lcom/oplus/ocs/camera/metadata/UConfigureKeys;->IS_OPLUS_PACKAGE:Lcom/oplus/ocs/camera/metadata/RequestKey;
